# shellcheck shell=bash
# Invocation behind output/evaluation/anonymisation_summary.json and
# anonymisation_report.csv (the privacy/intelligibility curve): 400 AMI test
# utterances, the first 25 usable ones in start-time order from each of the
# 16 test meetings, 14 speakers, at alphas 0.5, 0.7, 0.8 and 0.9.
#
# Job 8917989 (au_anon2), 2026-09-28, educ-intract, an NVIDIA L40S on
# htc-g078, at code 6f9bf56 with a clean tree, as its environment record and
# the summary's run_metadata say. It ran the multi-meeting preset and wrote to
# ${DATA}/speech_transcription_env/output/evaluation/audit2026/anon_multi.
# A 12-utterance pre-flight at alpha 0.8 (job 8913992, ANON_LIMIT=12
# ANON_ALPHAS=0.8, into audit2026/preflight_anon) ran before it.
#
# The speaker embeddings were taken from pyannote/wespeaker-voxceleb-resnet34-LM
# loaded directly, not through the diarisation pipeline that bundles it. A test
# had overwritten the cached config.yaml of pyannote/speaker-diarization-3.1
# on ARC, so the pipeline failed to load ("could not reuse the diarisation
# pipeline ('name')" on stderr) and the benchmark fell back to the model
# itself; that is why the summary's embedding_model lacks the "(via the
# diarisation pipeline)" suffix. Once the cache was restored, job 8976304
# loaded the pipeline and gave its embedding model and the directly loaded one
# the same four random 3-second waveforms on the CPU. Both are
# PyannoteAudioPretrainedSpeakerEmbedding instances of the same model and
# weights, and their embeddings were bit-identical (largest absolute
# difference 0.0), so the fallback did not change what was measured.
#
# Job 8781723 (2026-09-12) ran this configuration earlier, into
# output/evaluation/anon_multimeeting on ARC, before the per-meeting cap was
# enforced: it took up to 42 utterances from one meeting and reached 13 of
# the 16 meetings (audit finding EPRIV-03). It is not committed and should
# not be used. The single-meeting configuration is recorded in
# hpc/runs/anonymisation_single_meeting.env.
#
# Reproduce (from the repository root on ARC), on the card type the original
# ran on:
#   ( set -a; . hpc/runs/anonymisation.env || exit 1; set +a
#     sbatch --account=educ-intract --gres=gpu:l40s:1 hpc/submit_anonymisation.sh )
#
# The preset fixes the utterance count, the alphas and the cap, and
# submit_anonymisation.sh refuses ANON_LIMIT, ANON_ALPHAS or ANON_PER_MEETING
# beside it. REPORT_DIR below sends a reproduction to its own directory under
# repro/, so it cannot overwrite the original in audit2026/anon_multi, and the
# job refuses a REPORT_DIR that already holds a summary unless
# ANON_OVERWRITE=1.
ANON_PRESET=multi-meeting
REPORT_DIR="${DATA}/speech_transcription_env/output/evaluation/repro/anonymisation"
